    <DataNode elementId="AT5G10300-MONOMER" textLabel="hydroxynitrile lyase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LFT6" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">This enzyme has hydroxynitrile lyase activity &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt;. It can catalyze a sterospecific reaction using (&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;)-mandelonitrile |CITS: [17907254]|, however this compound has not been reported in Arabidopsis and is not likely to be a natural substrate. A wide varierty of compounds including aliphatic and aromatic aldehydes as well as ketones can be enantioselectively transformed into the corresponding R-cyanohydrins by this enzyme &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; but its &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; biological role has not yet been determined |CITS: [17907254]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G10300-MONOMER" />
